{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"a2e91cafa (+ 86b3c2283); 37/37 passing; status ok (was timeout). Three root causes: (1) grit upload-pack v2 returned after sending 'ready' instead of streaming the pack inline, deadlocking real-git over the stateful file transport (subtest 33 setup fetch) — fixed by threading stateless_rpc through serve_loop/process_one_v2_request/cmd_fetch and falling through to the packfile when ready & not stateless; (2) grit index-pack rejected --pack_header=<v>,<n> that real git's fetch-pack passes — now reconstructs the consumed 12-byte PACK header before the stdin body; (3) the --no-local --bundle-uri clone's v2 fetch sent no 'have' lines, so subtests 17/19/20 lacked 'clone> have <tip>' — added a haves param to write_v2_fetch_request and a local_negotiation_haves() helper (bundles/heads/tags/HEAD, peeled, honoring --negotiation-tip, skipped when shallow). Regression-checked isolated: t5510 215/215, t5552 6/6, t5701 25/25, t5555 10/10, t5601 111/115 & t5703 18/26 unchanged from baseline."}